    "description": "Two serialized SPQR states (PqRatchetState protobuf, the bytes libsignal stores in SessionStructure field 15 pq_ratchet_state) copied byte-for-byte from the spqr crate regression test for libcrux issue 1275. Per the upstream test, they were produced by running two parties in lockstep (A sends one message, B receives it, B sends one message, A receives it) for 30 steps, using a libcrux-ml-kem version whose portable backend serialized the encapsulation state with big-endian 16-bit words. Decoded by this agent: state_a = negotiation finished (no version_negotiation field), Chain direction A2B, current_epoch 0, V1 state HeaderSent (send_ek role) at epoch 1. state_b = Chain direction B2A, current_epoch 1, V1 state Ct1Sampled (send_ct role) at epoch 1; its stored 2080-byte encapsulation state has its error2 region (bytes 1536..2047 of the state) in big-endian order, for example the first words read 00 01 / 00 02 / ff ff. The upstream test loads both and runs 20 more lockstep steps (steps 30..49), asserting that each message key the sender gets equals the key the receiver gets; the test passes only if the receiver of B ct2 data can decapsulate, which requires the byte-swap fix described in spec/protocol/spqr/mlkem-incremental.md. The test uses fresh OS randomness, so there are no fixed expected outputs; use these as state-import inputs and as a self-consistency check.",
    "upstream_repo": "https://github.com/signalapp/SparsePostQuantumRatchet",
